{#
  module/Books/view/books/blog/index.phtml.

  Two oddities of the original, both reproduced rather than repaired:

  - the "New post" button has **no href**. It is an `<a class="btn btn-primary">` with
    nothing to click, behind an isAllowed() check, so only a blog contributor sees the
    dead control.
  - the excerpt is truncated *before* it is parsed, so the Markdown handed to the
    parser is frequently cut mid-list or mid-paragraph and the `...` lands inside
    whatever element it fell in. That is what the page shows today.

  `markdown` here and `markdown_safe` on the post page is the original's own
  inconsistency; App\Twig\MarkdownExtension::markdownSafe() records why both exist.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}
{% import 'schoenstatt/_entity-format.html.twig' as format %}
{% import 'books/_blog-front-matter.html.twig' as blog %}

{% block content %}
{% if is_allowed('route/blog/create') %}<p class="pull-right"><a class="btn btn-primary">{{ translate('New post') }}</a>
{% endif %}
{% for post in objects %}
<h2>{{ format.entity('blog-post', post) }}</h2>
    {{ blog.front_matter(post) }}
    {{ truncate_by_width(post.markdownText, 1000)|markdown }}
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
